{"strongs": "H4150", "word": "מוֺעֵד", "translit": "mo.ed", "root": "מועד", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "appointed time, place, meeting", "definition": "מוֺעֵד 223 noun masculine Ps 102:14 appointed time, place, meeting ; ׳ מ Exod 9:5 + 183 t.; מֹעֵד Deut 31:10 מוֺעֲדוֺ Num 9:2 + 2 t.; מֹעֲדוֺ Lam 2:6 + 3 t. + 5 t. suffixes; plural מוֺעֲדִים Dan 12:7 + 6 t.; מֹעֲדִים Zech 8:19 ; 1Chr 23:31 מוֺעֲדוֺת 2Chr 8:13 construct מֹועֲדֵי Lev 23:2 + 6 t.; מֹעֲדֵי Lev 23:44 suffixes מוֺעֲדַי Ezek 44:24 מֹעֲדֵיכֶם Num 15:3 + 6 t. suffixes; — 1. appointed time: \\ \\ a. in general with prefix לְ , at an or the appointed time Gen 18:14 ; Exod 13:10 ( J ), Exod 23:15 ; Exod 34:18 ; Josh 8:14 (all J E ), Gen 17:21 ; Gen 21:2 ( P ), 1Sam 9:24 ; 1Sam 13:8 (after אשׁר insert either אָמַר ᵐ5 ᵑ7 or שָׂם Dr ), v 1Sam 13:11 ; 2Kgs 4:16 ; 2Kgs 4:17 ; Hab 2:3 ; Dan 8:19 ; Dan 11:27 ; Dan 11:29 ; Dan 11:35 דוד ׳ למ at he time appointed with David 1Sam 20:35 ( Thes SS place appointed ); with prefix בְּ Hos 2:11 ; Lev 23:4 ; Num 9:2 ; Num 9:3 ; Num 9:7 ; Num 9:13 ; Num 28:2 ( P ); with מִן 2Sam 20:5 מ ׳ עַד עֵת 2Sam 24:15 unto the time appointed (but dubious, see Dr ); with verbs ׳ בא מ Ps 102:14 ׳ לקח מ Ps 75:3 ׳ שׂים מ Exod 9:5 ( J ); ׳ העביר המ Jer 46:17 the stork ׳ ידעה מ Jer 8:7 knows her appointed time ; צאתך ׳ מ Deut 16:6 time of thy going forth (from Egypt). \\ \\ b. in particular (compare Exod 13:10 ; Exod 23:15 ; Exod 34:18 ), sacred season , RV usually set feast or appointed season (wider than חַג , which was only a feast celebrated by a pilgrimage ), ׳ יוֺם (ימי) מ day \\ \\ \\ ( s ) of appointed season (i.e. festivals ) Hos 9:5 ; Hos 12:10 ; Lam 2:7 ; Lam 2:22 singular indefinite Lam 1:4 of the feast of booths Deut 31:10 || חג חדשׁ שׁבת Hos 2:13 || שׁבת Lam 2:6 usually plural יהוה ׳ מ Lev 23:2 ; Lev 23:4 ; Lev 23:37 ; Lev 23:44 ( P ), 2Chr 2:3 ; Ezra 3:5 with suffixes referring to ׳ י Lev 23:2 ( P ); ׳ בּמ Num 15:3 ; Num 29:39 ( P ), Ezek 36:38 ; Ezek 46:9 קרית ׳ מ city of our solemnities (sacred seasons) Isa 33:20 טובים ׳ למ Zech 8:19 || שׁבתות Ezek 44:24 || חדשׁים Isa 1:14 ; 1Chr 23:31 ; 2Chr 8:13 ; 2Chr 31:3 ; Neh 10:34 || חנים Ezek 46:11 חגים חדשׁים Ezek 45:17 || ראשׁי חָדְשֵׁכֶם Num 10:10 ( P ). — Notes. It is most probable that in Gen 1:14 ( P ), where ׳ מ || אֹתֹת , the reference is to the sacred seasons as fixed by moon's appearance; and so also ׳ עשׂה ירח למ he made the moon for sacred seasons Ps 104:19 , although many Lexicons & Commentaries refer these to the seasons of the year. — למועד מועדים וחצי Dan 12:7 for a set time, times, and a half = 3 1/2 appointed times = half the prophetic week of years, compare Br MP 453 f. — ׳ ויאכלו את המ they ate throughout the sacred season (of Maƒƒoth ) 2Chr 30:22 AV RV , but Thes SS Be Ke Öttli they ate the offerings of the sacred season ; ᵐ5 וַיְכַלּוּ . 2. appointed meeting: לְכָלחַֿי ׳ בֵּית מ Job 30:23 house of meeting for every living (of She'ol); ׳ קְרִאֵי מ Num 16:2 ( P ) called to the assembly = קְרִאֵי הָעֵדָה ; ׳ קרא עלי מ Lam 1:15 called a festal meeting against me ; ׳ בקרב מ Ps 74:4 in the midst of thine assembly ; הַר מוֺעֵד Isa 14:13 mount of meeting or assembly (of the gods; the mountain of the gods in the extreme north, the oriental Olympus, Persian Alborg , Hindu Meru , Babylon. Aralli , compare Len Origines ii, ch. ix ). 3. appointed place: \\ \\ a. the temple, || שׂכּוֺ Lam 2:6 , ׳ נוּגֵי ממ afflicted (and driven) from the place of assembly Zeph 3:18 (compare Br MP 225 ). \\ \\ b. synagogues, כָּלמֿוֺעֲדֵיאֵֿל בָּאָרֶץ all the appointed places of El in the land Ps 74:8 = בֵּית וַעַד Sota Ps 9:15 . 4. appointed sign, signal , Judg 20:38 . 5. אֹהֶל מוֺעֵד tent of meeting (of God with his people: see יָעַד Niph`al 1 ); the sacred tent of the Exodus (see אֹהֶל 3 ) Exod 33:7 (twice in verse); Num 12:4 ; Deut 31:14 (twice in verse) ( E ), Num 11:16 ( J ); often in P , as Exod 27:21 ; Exod 29:4 ; Lev 1:1 ; Lev 1:3 ; Josh 18:1 ; Josh 19:51 , etc. (131 t.)>; elsewhere only 1Sam 2:22 b (omitted by ᵐ5 ), 1Kgs 8:4 = 2Chr 5:5 ; 1Chr 6:17 ; 1Chr 9:21 ; 1Chr 23:32 ; 1Chr 2:3 ; 1Chr 2:6 ; 1Chr 2:13 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3608')\">BDB3608</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H4150')\">H4150</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3607')\">BDB3607</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3609')\">BDB3609</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>מוֺעֵד</bdbheb><sub>223</sub> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Ps 102:14\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"102\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"102\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(19,102,14)\">Ps 102:14</ref></sup> <highlightword>appointed time, place, meeting</highlightword>; <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>מ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 9:5\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(2,9,5)\">Exod 9:5</ref> + 183 t.; <bdbheb>מֹעֵד</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 31:10\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(5,31,10)\">Deut 31:10</ref> <bdbheb>מוֺעֲדוֺ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Num 9:2\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(4,9,2)\">Num 9:2</ref> + 2 t.; <bdbheb>מֹעֲדוֺ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lam 2:6\" b=\"25\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(25,2,6)\">Lam 2:6</ref> + 3 t. + 5 t. suffixes; plural <bdbheb>מוֺעֲדִים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Dan 12:7\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(27,12,7)\">Dan 12:7</ref> + 6 t.; <bdbheb>מֹעֲדִים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Zech 8:19\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(38,8,19)\">Zech 8:19</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Chr 23:31\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(13,23,31)\">1Chr 23:31</ref> <bdbheb>מוֺעֲדוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Chr 8:13\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(14,8,13)\">2Chr 8:13</ref> construct <bdbheb>מֹועֲדֵי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lev 23:2\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\